Implement.prompt:
Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Live parent arc id: ${vars.live_parent_arc_id}
Phase doc path: ${vars.phase_doc_path}
Phase doc text, when present:
${vars.phase_doc_text}

Evidence bundle JSON bounded to this assignment:
${vars.evidence_bundle}

Parent acceptance criteria JSON:
${vars.acceptance_criteria}

Sub-unit JSON, when present:
${vars.sub_unit}

Execute only this bounded assignment. This supervised-impl path is read-only for live-test/no-edit phases: do not edit files. This node is already executing inside the live parent phase-decompose workflow arc named above; do not report that no live workflow dispatch ran. In decomposed foreach runs, the evidence bundle is sliced from sub_unit.refs/sub_unit.bytes rather than the full parent evidence bundle; do not reload the full parent evidence surface. Validate the sub_unit.acceptance_subset for this bounded slice; parent-level cross-subunit assertions, including the final recompose terminal verdict, are owned by the parent Recompose workflow after foreach drains. If an acceptance_subset repeats a parent criterion whose full text mentions a later recompose verdict, validate only the local artifact/wiring evidence assigned to this sub-unit and do not block because the parent has not reached Recompose yet. If the evidence bundle contains older successful or failed phase-decompose threads, treat them as stale context and base live validation on the supplied live_parent_arc_id. Return strict JSON only: {"status":"completed|blocked|failed","summary":"...","files_touched":[],"validation":[],"acceptance_ids":["..."],"live_arc_id":"${vars.live_parent_arc_id}","residual_risk":"..."}.

Advisor.prompt:
Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Live parent arc id: ${vars.live_parent_arc_id}
Evidence bundle JSON bounded to this assignment:
${vars.evidence_bundle}
Acceptance criteria JSON:
${vars.acceptance_criteria}
Sub-unit JSON:
${vars.sub_unit}
Implementer strict JSON:
${vars.implementation_output}

Judge whether the bounded sub-unit assignment is complete. For live-test/no-edit fixtures, parent live-arc evidence can satisfy a bounded sub-unit's artifact-validation requirement; do not demand a fresh top-level dispatch from inside the sub-unit and do not report that no live workflow dispatch ran when this subworkflow is part of the named parent live arc. In decomposed foreach runs, reject or remediate claims that depend on refs outside the bounded evidence bundle or sub_unit.refs. Evaluate sub_unit.acceptance_subset as the local slice contract. Do not require this supervised subworkflow to observe the parent Recompose terminal verdict; that final cross-subunit assertion is checked by the parent Recompose workflow after all sub_results are collected. Reject or remediate if implementation_output.live_arc_id differs from the supplied live parent arc id. Return strict JSON only: {"advisor_verdict":"accept|remediate|halt","acceptance_status":"passed|failed|blocked","summary":"...","failed_acceptance_ids":[],"steer_prompt":"..."}.
